      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cottondale%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cottondale was a site where the Knights of Labor organized drives in the late 1880s, and where Mother Jones worked in 1904 studying conditions for women and children.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cottondale%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Children’s author Aileen Kilgore Henderson, known for her works on rural life, resides in Cottondale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
